# Networking Task

Task: Restrict SSH access for the existing user `{{restricted_user}}`.

Configure the OpenSSH daemon so that, for the user `{{restricted_user}}` only:

- every SSH session is forced to run the command `{{forced_command}}` (ForceCommand);
- TCP forwarding is disabled.

All other accounts must keep the default SSH behavior. The SSH service must remain running with a valid configuration, and the restrictions must persist across reboots.
